  "answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative led by Marcus Cole, launching in Q3 2023 with a kickoff on July 15th. The project aims to enhance security and accessibility using AI algorithms, with initial findings suggesting a 20% efficiency increase. Key milestones include securing a strategic partnership with TechInnovate, receiving a $2M budget approval, and successfully completing the testing phase for a secure file sharing prototype. The team is expanding with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture. Current phases involve gathering R&D ideas for data visualization, planning user interface enhancements for October, and seeking stakeholder feedback on the prototype by November. A celebration for the testing milestone is scheduled for October 10th."
